in this video i'll break down the golden  fishing rod and animal crossing new  horizons  i'll explain how to get it how long you  have to wait what it does and most  importantly  is it worth it people of the internet  retrorecontour here and welcome to  another animal crossing new horizons  video  if we're meeting for the first time i'm  just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and today we're talking all  about the golden fishing rod and animal  crossing new horizons  so there's actually two ways to get a  golden fishing rod one way is really  easy and the other  way takes a lot more time but will  ultimately be better for you in the long  run  the easy way is through gifting or  trading that's right you can have a  friend who's already  unlocked the goldenrod send one straight  to your mailbox  alternatively you could also trade for  one through some of the animal crossing  discord groups such as nukazon  there are some significant downsides to  this however you see if you're just  gifted the item you won't actually  receive the recipe which means when your  goldenrod eventually breaks  and yes they really do break but more on  that in a second but when it does break  you won't be able to make another to  replace it so you'd be right back to  where you started  that being said there is another  downside to receiving golden tools as  gifts  first you won't actually be working for  and earning the goldenrod how the game  intended  don't get me wrong i'm glad the gifting  option is there especially for younger  kids who may not be able to play during  the hours required to actually unlock  the rod  in game but i actually had someone gift  me a golden axe without me  even asking might i had and while it was  an awesome gift it definitely took that  sense of achievement away from  actually earning the reward so if you  only want the golden fishing rod then by  all means trade for it find a friend  who'll give it to you  but if you want that sense of  achievement then you'll want to stay  tuned maybe it's just me who knows but i  actually  love working towards in-game goals this  is absolutely one of those things that's  entirely  up to you though okay so how do you  unlock it for  real the second way of unlocking the  goldenrod and what most would say is the  true way of doing it  you have to catch every fish in the game  that's right  every single fish now that we're right  around the one year mark of animal  crossings launched that means that both  northern and southern hemisphere players  have now had a chance to catch  every fish in the game without time  travel  one important note here regarding the  golden rod is that you do not have to  turn the fish into the museum  personally i always turn my first catch  of each fish into the museum anyway but  if you're someone who doesn't bother  with the museum then  what's wrong with you i'm kidding i'm  kidding regardless  turning a fish into the museum is not a  requirement you just have to make sure  that each fish shows up in your critter  pedia  using the critter pedia makes it very  easy to check and see how many fish you  still need  from there i'd recommend using the  animal crossing wiki page or a mobile  app such as  acnh.guide seriously awesome app  check it out if you're new to the game  you should know that fish change with  both the time of day  and the current month of your island  there are even certain fish that can  only be caught when it's raining or  from the pier on your island all of this  information for each fish can be found  on those sites i mentioned  i'll be sure and link them in the  description as well important note here  you do not need to catch  all of the deep sea creatures in order  to receive the golden rod it's fish  only for this one once you catch your  final fish though  well you'll receive a fun little message  in game which i won't spoil here but for  me  after that it was a little unclear how i  actually  get the golden rod and even digging  around online i couldn't really find an  exact answer to what i was looking for  it's part of the reason i made this  video here  once you catch all the fish what do you  do from there luckily the solution is  rather simple for me i just needed to  wait until the next day and then  inside my mailbox i found this special  letter from the faraway museum  again you still don't have to turn the  fish into the museum they congratulated  me on catching every fish and inside  was the recipe for the golden fishing  rod from there go to your nearest  crafting bench and you can immediately  craft the rod which requires one  standard fishing rod and one gold nugget  to craft  so there you have it your reward for  catching every fish in the game is the  golden  fishing rod but is it really worth all  that time invested  there's pros and cons here on the  positive side you have a specially  colored tool that shows just how much of  a dedicated fisherman you are  and golden tools are the most durable in  the game however they actually do have a  set lifespan and will eventually break  they do last quite a long time and my  goldenrod has yet to break i can't say  for certain but i've seen reports online  that you can get as many as  200 uses out of the golden tools if any  of you out there know the exact amount  let everyone know down in the comments  below i'd love to know if there's been  an  actual number confirmed for how many  times you can use the golden fishing rod  for me i wish the golden tools were  unbreakable but i certainly don't regret  going for it the truth is i would have  wanted to catch all the fish  anyway even if it was just a check mark  in my nook app so i just see the golden  rod as kind of like a visual indicator  of the achievement that i completed  if you're new to animal crossing new  horizons i have a full beginners  playlist here on the right side of the  screen  as always thank you guys so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

